From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:34:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(claude-sdk): opt into Claude Code's WebSearch and
 WebFetch

The claude-sdk harness pins Claude Code's built-in tools to Skill and
ToolSearch, so a claude-sdk agent cannot use Claude's own web search even
on a first-party subscription. Omnigent's web_search builtin needs a
separate search backend and key, and is not the same tool.

Add executor.config.native_tools, accepting WebSearch and WebFetch. The
named tools join the CLI's base tool set. They stay off allowed_tools so
every call still reaches the TOOL_CALL policy gate; in auto mode the gate
then approves them without a human prompt, as it does for Omnigent's own
tools. WebSearch is withheld when ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL points at a
non-Anthropic gateway, which cannot serve the nested web_search request;
Bedrock, Vertex and Foundry gate it themselves.

Carried on custom so claude-sdk chat sessions can search the web;
not upstream yet (proposal pending). Drop once it lands upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
